WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.267
-Pro-Trump election deniers

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:05.000
have won GOP primaries
across the country,

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.968
which could put them
in positions of power

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:09.167
in swing states during
the next presidential election.

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:11.467
Meanwhile, a key Trump
White House official

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.934
has been subpoenaed
by a federal grand jury

00:00:13.934 --> 00:00:15.934
as the Justice Department
investigates the events

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:18.133
surrounding the coup attempt
on January 6th.

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.501
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:24.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.133
It's never been more important
than it is right now

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:29.200
to investigate
and hold accountable the people

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.467
who nearly toppled our democracy
on January 6th,

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.968
because, as we have said
many times on this show,

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:36.734
they came very close, and they
will absolutely do it again

00:00:36.734 --> 00:00:38.000
if they get the chance.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.167
Trump is already in the process
of setting up

00:00:40.167 --> 00:00:42.501
another coup attempt
by attempting to put loyalists

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:45.000
in positions of power
across the country.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.501
-Former President Trump's
influence

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:47.734
is being put to the test,

00:00:47.734 --> 00:00:50.534
endorsing several
so-called election deniers,

00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:52.968
Republican candidates
who support his false claims

00:00:52.968 --> 00:00:54.567
of a stolen election.

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:57.467
-Tonight's primaries testing
former President Trump's power

00:00:57.467 --> 00:00:58.934
over the Republican Party

00:00:58.934 --> 00:01:01.767
and nowhere more so
than here in Arizona,

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:04.133
a state Trump lost
and where he has now waged

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:06.734
an all-out assault
on the GOP establishment

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:09.834
that refused to go along
with his false election claims.

00:01:09.834 --> 00:01:12.167
Up and down the ballot,
Trump-endorsed candidates

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:15.234
who deny the legitimacy
of the 2020 election.

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:17.367
Arizona is a revenge state
for Trump.

00:01:17.367 --> 00:01:19.567
He's endorsed candidates
from the U.S. Senate

00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:21.834
all the way down
to the state legislature

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:23.334
and even the secretary of state,

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:26.234
who would oversee the next
presidential election.

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:29.734
-I'm sorry. Arizona is
a revenge state for him?

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:31.601
What's he going to do,
make us live there?

00:01:31.601 --> 00:01:33.501
Oh, sure,
it's sunny and beautiful,

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:36.767
but just try to order a pizza
after 9:00 p.m.

00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:38.367
Speak of the sun,

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:40.534
make sure you find
a dermatologist you really like,

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:41.968
because you're going to see
her more

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:44.133
than you see your own family.

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:46.267
Our head writer is from Arizona,

00:01:46.267 --> 00:01:48.934
and he obviously
has some issues.

00:01:48.934 --> 00:01:52.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:55.300
Nothing says divider
instead of uniter

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:59.200
more than a former president
with a revenge state.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.400
You lost an election.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.067
Stop acting like Liam Neeson

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:04.234
threatening to get
his daughter back.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:06.734
"I have a very particular
set of skills.

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:10.067
I can shank a golf ball
90 yards.

00:02:10.067 --> 00:02:13.300
I can drink three Diet Cokes
in one sitting, and that's it.

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:16.701
So in the end, the end,
it's just the two skills.

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:18.801
And as I say them out loud,
I'm not sure how either

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.434
is going to help me
get my daughter back.

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:23.334
So this -- this might be
one of those occasions

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:25.234
where you just drop her off
back at the house.

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:26.367
Would that work?"

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:28.000
[ Dial tone ]

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.200
"Hello? Hello?

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:34.934
Good news, Don Jr.
You're my new favorite."

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:39.400
"You're still number four, Eric.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.834
I don't want to
have to explain it."

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:43.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:49.501
Seriously, why does Donald Trump
have a revenge state?

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:51.400
Is this the first time
a former president

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:54.067
has gone on a, quote, revenge
tour after leaving office?

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:56.300
Like, usually, ex-presidents
retire to a quiet life

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.434
of paid speaking gigs
and celebrity golf tournaments.

00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:01.934
I don't remember William Howard
Taft going from town to town

00:03:01.934 --> 00:03:04.033
looking for anyone
who didn't vote for him in 1912

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:06.167
so he could kick them
in the [bleep]

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:07.868
"Hey, you with
the Woodrow Wilson button,

00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:09.167
I'm going to fight you.

00:03:09.167 --> 00:03:12.400
I just need to squeeze
out of this bathtub first."

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.234
By the way, Taft never got stuck
in the White House bathtub.

00:03:16.234 --> 00:03:18.701
That's just a myth you learned
in middle school
for some reason.

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:21.100
What a bummer to climb to
the heights of the presidency,

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.567
the most powerful position
in the world,

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:24.467
and all anyone remembers
about you is a rumor

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:27.000
some jerk made up about you
getting stuck in a bathtub.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.868
That would be like if, instead
of remembering Albert Einstein

00:03:29.868 --> 00:03:31.834
for his theory of relativity,
all anyone knew about him

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:36.267
was that one time he [bleep]
his pants at a Panera Bread.

00:03:36.267 --> 00:03:38.868
And that was today's
dubious product placement

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:42.267
for Panera Bread.

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:45.033
So Trump is on a revenge tour,

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:47.200
crisscrossing the country
to back candidates

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.868
who, if they get into office,
will help him

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:50.601
steal the election again
in 2024,

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:53.601
because he has all but declared
that he's running again.

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:55.400
He keeps dropping
not-so-subtle hints,

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:57.767
including at his golf course
in New Jersey last week.

00:03:57.767 --> 00:04:00.634
-Mr. President, are you planning
to announce soon for the --

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:02.934
-Oh, you're gonna be so happy.

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:05.868
-Oof. What was that low,
gravelly voice?

00:04:05.868 --> 00:04:07.667
If someone came up to me
on a golf course

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:11.434
looking like that, hunched over,
all hoarse and sweaty and said,

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:14.167
"You're gonna be so happy,"

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:16.701
I would assume he was selling
discount golf balls

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:18.567
he found in the woods.

00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:21.501
"Got a perfectly good Titleist.

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:24.100
Also, you want to see
a dead squirrel?

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:26.300
I can show it to you.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:28.601
You want to see a dead squirrel?

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.968
A bird ate its eyes.
Come on, dead squirrel?"

00:04:31.968 --> 00:04:37.033
So Trump is very much set on
trying the coup again in 2024.

00:04:37.033 --> 00:04:38.434
And even if he doesn't run,

00:04:38.434 --> 00:04:40.701
or if he loses the GOP primary
to someone else,

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.167
the loyalists
and election deniers

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:44.534
he's trying to put in place will
undoubtedly use their power,

00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:46.968
if they win in November,
to prevent any Democrat

00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:48.400
from winning
an election ever again.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.901
And now that they've won
their GOP primaries,

00:04:50.901 --> 00:04:53.601
these pro-Trump election deniers
are just one more step away

00:04:53.601 --> 00:04:55.167
from taking key positions
of power

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:56.934
in swing states
all across the country.

00:04:56.934 --> 00:04:59.667
In Arizona, for example, a slate
of pro-Trump election deniers

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:01.200
have either already won

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.133
or are currently leading
in GOP primaries

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:05.601
for federal and state offices,
including governor.

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:07.767
Kari Lake,
the candidate currently leading

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:09.000
the GOP primary for governor,

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.901
has said
some truly insane [bleep]

00:05:10.901 --> 00:05:12.434
about the 2020 election.

00:05:12.434 --> 00:05:16.601
-Anybody who was involved
in that corrupt, shady,

00:05:16.601 --> 00:05:20.334
shoddy election of 2020,

00:05:20.334 --> 00:05:22.934
lock them up.

00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:25.000
I refuse to stop
talking about it

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.901
until our elected officials
stand up and do something.

00:05:27.901 --> 00:05:32.534
We want people to be arrested,
prosecuted, and thrown in jail.

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:34.801
We have this illegitimate
President Biden

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.501
who's allowing it to happen.

00:05:36.501 --> 00:05:38.234
But the fake news
wants us to think

00:05:38.234 --> 00:05:42.300
that that guy got
81 million votes.

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:46.901
[ Crowd booing ]

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:48.667
Okay.

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:51.467
-I love how Trump supporters
keep insisting it's impossible

00:05:51.467 --> 00:05:53.634
that Joe Biden
got 81 million votes.

00:05:53.634 --> 00:05:55.267
You know how he got
that many votes --

00:05:55.267 --> 00:05:58.267
by running against Donald Trump.

00:05:58.267 --> 00:06:00.167
Okay?

00:06:00.167 --> 00:06:02.133
It's like if you told me --

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:05.601
if you told me
the Warriors scored 160 points,

00:06:05.601 --> 00:06:07.901
I might also be suspicious
until you told me

00:06:07.901 --> 00:06:10.400
they were playing the Knicks,
and then, you know...

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.234
And, look, you guys, I know
basketball isn't in season,

00:06:13.234 --> 00:06:15.300
but we're in a bit of a jam
here at "Late Night,"

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:17.634
because our summertime
whipping boys, the Mets,

00:06:17.634 --> 00:06:19.567
are currently in first place.

00:06:19.567 --> 00:06:21.868
And if I've -- Yeah.
[ Applause ]

00:06:21.868 --> 00:06:24.033
And if I've learned anything
from my time in New York,

00:06:24.033 --> 00:06:26.868
it's that if the Mets are
in first place on August 4th,

00:06:26.868 --> 00:06:29.467
they're on lock to win
the World Series.

00:06:32.067 --> 00:06:33.834
The other day, a member
of my crew said to me,

00:06:33.834 --> 00:06:36.767
"Hey, we're 3 1/2 up,
with only 58 games to play."

00:06:36.767 --> 00:06:37.968
And all I could say was,

00:06:37.968 --> 00:06:41.868
"Why do you keep
letting yourself get hurt?"

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.901
But here's what's truly ironic
and revealing

00:06:43.901 --> 00:06:46.434
about Kari Lake's lead
in the Arizona GOP primary.

00:06:46.434 --> 00:06:49.300
She was actually trailing
on Tuesday night

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:50.701
before more votes were counted

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:52.467
and put her over the top
by Wednesday morning,

00:06:52.467 --> 00:06:55.100
the exact kind of thing
election deniers

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:57.901
would lose their [bleep] over
if it was the other side.

00:06:57.901 --> 00:07:00.634
Remember when Trump
kept complaining over and over

00:07:00.634 --> 00:07:02.801
about what he claimed
were mysterious ballot dumps

00:07:02.801 --> 00:07:05.200
supposedly putting Biden
in the lead overnight?

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:07.701
That's just normal vote
counting. That's how it works.

00:07:07.701 --> 00:07:09.467
But Trump thought
it was suspicious.

00:07:09.467 --> 00:07:12.267
-This election was over,
and then they did dumps.

00:07:12.267 --> 00:07:15.801
They call them dumps,
big, massive dumps.

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:20.601
In Michigan and Pennsylvania
and all over.

00:07:20.601 --> 00:07:21.834
-You guys remember that?

00:07:21.834 --> 00:07:23.534
You remember the leader
of the free world

00:07:23.534 --> 00:07:25.534
complaining about big,
massive dumps,

00:07:25.534 --> 00:07:29.200
like -- like he's working
in the elephant enclosure

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.300
at the Bronx Zoo?

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:36.300
"Oh, Goddamn it. Who let
the elephants eat cheesecake?

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.934
It's going to take me days
to clean up."

00:07:41.334 --> 00:07:44.033
You know how --

00:07:44.033 --> 00:07:46.467
You know how when you go
to a presidential library,

00:07:46.467 --> 00:07:48.534
they usually have
an interactive section

00:07:48.534 --> 00:07:50.834
where you can press a button
and hear some original audio,

00:07:50.834 --> 00:07:54.667
like one of FDR's fireside chats
or JFK's inaugural speech?

00:07:54.667 --> 00:07:57.000
I don't think Trump deserves
a presidential library,

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.200
but if he gets one,
I hope the interactive feature

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:03.100
is a toilet that uses his voice
whenever you flush.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:07.868
-Welcome to the Donald J. Trump
Presidential Library.

00:08:07.868 --> 00:08:12.667
Flush the handle to begin
your journey through history.

00:08:12.667 --> 00:08:14.667
[ Toilet flushes ]

00:08:14.667 --> 00:08:16.367
-They did dumps.

00:08:16.367 --> 00:08:19.501
They call them dumps,
big, massive dumps.

00:08:19.501 --> 00:08:21.601
-So now --

00:08:21.601 --> 00:08:23.934
So now, all of a sudden --

00:08:23.934 --> 00:08:26.334
all of a sudden,
big, massive dumps

00:08:26.334 --> 00:08:28.267
that change the race overnight
are totally cool,

00:08:28.267 --> 00:08:30.234
as long as they benefit
the pro-Trump candidates,

00:08:30.234 --> 00:08:32.667
which just shows you
that it's all [bleep]

00:08:32.667 --> 00:08:34.767
a fabricated pretext
designed to justify

00:08:34.767 --> 00:08:36.067
whatever outcome they want.

00:08:36.067 --> 00:08:38.534
And that is why we need to
root these people out now

00:08:38.534 --> 00:08:40.701
before they get into positions
that would give them power

00:08:40.701 --> 00:08:42.534
over our elections in 2024.

00:08:42.534 --> 00:08:45.534
Arguably an even scarier example
is the GOP's nominee

00:08:45.534 --> 00:08:47.300
for secretary of state
in Arizona,

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:49.167
a position
that directly supervises

00:08:49.167 --> 00:08:50.534
the state's elections.

00:08:50.534 --> 00:08:53.601
-Election denialism is still
coursing through the veins

00:08:53.601 --> 00:08:55.067
of this Republican Party.

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:56.834
No better example
than in Arizona.

00:08:56.834 --> 00:08:59.567
The results of last night's
elections make clear

00:08:59.567 --> 00:09:02.267
for secretary of state,
for example, Mark Finchem.

00:09:02.267 --> 00:09:04.601
He is a Republican legislator
in Arizona,

00:09:04.601 --> 00:09:06.534
one of the leading voices
in denying

00:09:06.534 --> 00:09:08.701
the results of the 2020 election

00:09:08.701 --> 00:09:10.901
that Joe Biden
won the state of Arizona.

00:09:10.901 --> 00:09:12.667
He is going to be
the Republican nominee

00:09:12.667 --> 00:09:15.267
for the secretary of state,
the top election official.

00:09:15.267 --> 00:09:17.234
-Trump's candidate,
Mark Finchem,

00:09:17.234 --> 00:09:19.701
who acknowledged having ties
to the Oath Keepers

00:09:19.701 --> 00:09:22.467
and was in Washington
on January 6th.

00:09:22.467 --> 00:09:25.334
-This is insane. We can't let
a guy who wanted to overthrow

00:09:25.334 --> 00:09:27.767
the last election
oversee future elections.

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:29.801
I wouldn't keep using Wally
as my cue card guy

00:09:29.801 --> 00:09:31.601
if he started undermining me

00:09:31.601 --> 00:09:33.100
by writing stuff
I didn't approve of,

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:34.367
like, "Wally is the best.

00:09:34.367 --> 00:09:37.033
He's the most popular.
He should host this show."

00:09:37.033 --> 00:09:38.634
Wait a second.

00:09:38.634 --> 00:09:40.801
[ Laughter ]

00:09:40.801 --> 00:09:42.400
Damn it!

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:45.334
Wally!

00:09:45.334 --> 00:09:48.234
I'd be mad, but what can I say?
I agree with you.

00:09:48.234 --> 00:09:50.434
You would be a better host.
Wait!

00:09:51.667 --> 00:09:53.534
Just stop it!

00:09:53.534 --> 00:09:56.200
[ Applause ]

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.400
The point is we need to
stop these people now,

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:01.367
which is why it is encouraging
to see the Justice Department

00:10:01.367 --> 00:10:03.734
stepping up its investigation
of the coup attempt.

00:10:03.734 --> 00:10:05.901
They're reportedly
asking witnesses about Trump

00:10:05.901 --> 00:10:07.434
as part of their investigation.

00:10:07.434 --> 00:10:09.234
And now a federal grand jury
has subpoenaed

00:10:09.234 --> 00:10:11.067
a senior
Trump White House official

00:10:11.067 --> 00:10:12.601
who was a key witness
to the events

00:10:12.601 --> 00:10:14.300
that led up to January 6th.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:16.634
-Now, it's a dramatic
development in the January 6th
investigation.

00:10:16.634 --> 00:10:17.801
A source tells CNN

00:10:17.801 --> 00:10:19.934
former Trump White House Counsel
Pat Cipollone

00:10:19.934 --> 00:10:22.834
has been subpoenaed
by a federal grand jury

00:10:22.834 --> 00:10:26.467
investigating efforts
to overturn the 2020 election.

00:10:26.467 --> 00:10:29.167
He's considered part of
Donald Trump's inner circle,

00:10:29.167 --> 00:10:31.801
and the move to subpoena him
signals an aggressive step

00:10:31.801 --> 00:10:33.501
by the Justice Department.

00:10:33.501 --> 00:10:35.634
It shows investigators
are looking at conduct

00:10:35.634 --> 00:10:39.133
directly related to Trump,
as well as his closest allies,

00:10:39.133 --> 00:10:41.467
efforts to overturn
his election defeat.

00:10:41.467 --> 00:10:44.100
-The subpoena is part of
the federal investigation

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.734
into the January 6th assault
on the Capitol

00:10:46.734 --> 00:10:49.267
and efforts to overturn
the 2020 election.

00:10:49.267 --> 00:10:53.734
Although it is not clear exactly
which grand jury called him.

00:10:53.734 --> 00:10:55.801
There are currently
two known grand juries,

00:10:55.801 --> 00:10:58.567
one looking at the scheme
to assemble fake electors

00:10:58.567 --> 00:11:00.367
and the other focused
specifically

00:11:00.367 --> 00:11:02.100
on the events of January 6th.

